  "category": "moving_head_beam",
  "description": "A Clay Paky Sharpy moving-head beam fixture. The rectangular base, about 40 by 11 by 34 units, carries the pan motor and a control panel with display and buttons on its rear, probably with carry handles on each side. Rising from the pan pivot is one side U-yoke arm carrying the tilt axle. The head is a boxy shell ending in a round lens barrel at the front. Pan covers 540 degrees on the base and tilt 250 degrees within the yoke, both DMX-driven, moving the whole head. The front has one lens over one light source, giving one dimmer cell. Colour, gobo and effect wheels, prism and frost are not modelled.",
